// CONFORMANCE-CASE
// spec: 09-identity-origin-extent
// facility: rule.ref.form [Ref-Form-Temporary]
// kind: negative
// expect: diag.borrow-of-non-place (static)
//
// A temporary (here, a call result) has no binding to outlive the
// statement; borrowing it directly is rejected. This particular
// shape -- a *plain* (non-resource) value-returning call -- correctly
// reports diag.borrow-of-non-place, not diag.borrow-of-temporary:
// spec/registry/diagnostics.md's own shared entry for the two
// distinguishes "a value" (this case; the interpreter represents a
// plain call result directly as a value, with no object identity to
// call a "temporary") from "a temporary" (an object-identity-bearing
// result -- see 09-identity-origin-extent/borrow_of_resource_
// temporary_rejected.cb for that exact case, which does report
// diag.borrow-of-temporary). An initial read of this interpreter's
// behavior mistook this correct distinction for a missing precision;
// re-verified and corrected (see impl/STATUS.md).

fn make() : i32
{
    5
}

fn main()
{
    auto r = &make();
}
